messages.body_plain:
First, your stan code doesn't compile because invgamma doesn't exist. It needs to be inv_gamma.

Second, I'm not clear on what you mean by "convergence of the estimations are not possible". With a iter=1000 run (which takes about 7mins on my machine), most parameters have a good ESS of about 500, with muP and muQ being the exceptions, so it looks like you'd need more iterations for those. Or are you saying that the posterior on one or more of the parameters doesn't mesh with the known true values (since you simulated the data)? Again, only muP and muQ look off from their true values in my iter=1000 run, which isn't surprising given the low ESS. Do you have a high iteration run that achieves good ESS/rhat for muP & muQ and still observe inconsistency between the posterior and known true values?

